"""
brickbreaker - Native ckb-next animation (v5).

A self-playing brick-breaker game with progressive levels, multi-hit bricks,
power-up drops, and multi-ball.

Copyright (c) 2026 Preston A. Elder <prez@neuromancy.net>.
Licensed under the MIT License -- see the LICENSE file in the project
repository for the full text.

Designed and refined by Preston A. Elder <prez@neuromancy.net>.
Code authored by Claude AI under Preston's direction.

Tested on a Corsair K70. Other ckb-next-supported keyboards should work
but key layouts may differ.

Install:
  Drop this file (executable) into your user-local ckb-next animations
  directory, then have the GUI re-scan its scripts. No sudo, no daemon
  restart, no GUI restart needed:

    mkdir -p ~/.local/share/ckb-next/animations
    cp brickbreaker ~/.local/share/ckb-next/animations/
    chmod +x ~/.local/share/ckb-next/animations/brickbreaker

  Then in ckb-next: Settings -> Animation Scripts -> Re-scan. The
  animation appears in the Lighting tab as "Brick Breaker".

  In the animation's Properties -> Settings -> Playback, enable
  "Start with mode" so the animation runs whenever the mode is active.
  Brick Breaker does NOT need "Start with key press" -- it does not
  read keypresses.

Numpad level counter:
  * 1-9:  num1..num9 lit cumulatively in green (tier 0)
  * 10-18: numlock lit + num1..num9 cumulating in yellow (tier 1)
  * 19-27: numlock+numslash + num1..num9 cumulating in orange (tier 2)
  * 28-36: numlock+numslash+numstar + num1..num9 in red (tier 3)
  * 37+:  saturated red pulse

Per-level scaling:
  * Ball speed scales: base * (1 + level_speed * (level-1))
  * Brick HP distribution shifts toward harder
  * Paddle speed STAYS FIXED -- AI gets less accurate at high levels.

Paddle physics (Arkanoid-style):
  * Ball horizontal velocity comes from TWO sources at paddle collision:
    1. Position contribution: where on paddle the ball hits (small effect)
    2. Paddle friction: paddle's own horizontal motion drags the ball
       (canonical formula: ball.vx += friction * paddle.vx)
  * Result is capped so the ball always retains substantial upward motion.
  * Speed bleeds back to base over ~3 seconds, so boosts don't accumulate.

AI strategy:
  * To deflect ball toward a target column, AI uses the SETUP-AND-GLIDE
    technique: positions paddle to the OPPOSITE side of desired deflection
    during setup phase, then slides through impact_x at impact time. The
    paddle's motion-velocity gets imparted to the ball.
  * AI naturally fails when ball is too fast for paddle to set up in time.

AI skill (rolled per game):
  * Each game restart rolls a new AI "player" with randomized skill from
    Beta(3, 3). Most AIs are average; very-bad and very-good AIs are rare.
  * Skill multipliers affect:
      paddle_speed_mult (0.4x..3.0x): how fast the paddle can move
      prediction_error_mult (5x..0.2x): how badly AI mispredicts the ball
      aim_strength_mult (0.3x..1.0x): how aggressively AI tries to aim
  * Result: each playthrough is a different character. Rare runs see a
    terrible AI that loses on level 1, or a brilliant AI that clears all
    36 levels.

Multi-hit bricks (color by remaining HP):
  hp=3 red, hp=2 yellow, hp=1 green.

Power-up drops (rate-limited; ~one per 20-30s):
  LONGER (green):       +1 paddle key
  SHORTER (red):        -1 paddle key (AI avoids)
  MULTIBALL (cyan):     +2 balls (cap 3)
  EXTRA_LIFE (magenta): +1 life (cap 4, the max)

Game flow:
  Miss (last ball gone) -> red flash -> life lost.
  0 lives -> red strobe -> reset to level 1.
  All bricks cleared -> rainbow strobe -> next level.

Parameters (all tunable in the ckb-next GUI):
  basespeed       Base ball speed at level 1, keys/sec
                  (default 60.0, range 20.0-200.0)
  maxspeed        Cap on ball speed at level 1 after friction boosts
                  (default 110.0, range 30.0-300.0)
  paddlespeed     Paddle movement speed; fixed across all levels
                  (default 110.0, range 20.0-300.0)
  paddlewidth     Starting paddle width in keys, before power-ups
                  (default 4, range 2-8)
  levelspeed      Fractional speed boost added per level beyond 1
                  (default 0.12, range 0.0-0.5; 0.12 = +12%/level)
  chaos           Randomness applied to ball deflection
                  (default 0.20, range 0.0-1.0)
  aimstrength     How aggressively the AI aims its returns
                  (default 0.50, range 0.0-1.0; further multiplied
                  by the per-game rolled AI skill)
  dropchance      Probability a destroyed brick drops a power-up
                  (default 0.5, range 0.0-1.0; 0 disables drops)
  dropcooldown    Minimum seconds between power-up drops
                  (default 25.0, range 5.0-120.0)
  paddlefriction  Fraction of paddle motion imparted to the ball
                  on contact (default 0.6, range 0.0-1.0)
  ballcolor       ARGB color of the ball (default ffffffff, white)
  paddlecolor     ARGB color of the paddle (default ff00ffff, cyan)
"""
